## Model card

- **Name:** GPT-5.6 Luna
- **Short description:** OpenAI’s GPT-5.6 Luna is a budget/efficiency-tier model for cost-sensitive, high-volume workloads, with 1.05M context and reasoning-effort controls.
- **Provider / access:** OpenAI API/ChatGPT/Codex surfaces (per metadata/docs). Local metadata lists `openai/gpt-5.6-luna` and `noFreeId` (with Codex quota note).
- **Release / knowledge:** Developer docs list knowledge cutoff February 16, 2026. Announcement page not accessible in this pass.
- **IDs:** `gpt-5.6-luna`.
- **Context window:** 1,050,000 context window; 922,000 maximum input tokens; 128,000 max output tokens (OpenAI developer docs).
- **Modalities:** Text and image input; text output (OpenAI developer docs).
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-10):** $0.20 / 1M input, $0.02 / 1M cached input, $1.20 / 1M output (OpenAI developer docs). Prompts >272K input priced at 2x input and 1.5x output for full request; cache writes billed at 1.25x uncached input.
- **Architecture:** Proprietary OpenAI model; architecture/parameter count not publicly disclosed.

